格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Obsidian bridge plugin for DSH","id":"gh:1333790823","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-obsidian","slug":"gxpppp/dsh-obsidian","topics":["deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","obsidian"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Obsidian bridge plugin for DSH"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-obsidian"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"`dsh-obsidian` is a host-only Obsidian integration for DeepSeek Harness (DSH). The main branch targe"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"ts DSH `0.1.2-alpha.2` exactly. Earlier prerelease lines are preserved as immutable legacy branches "},{"id":"p3s3","text":".1.2-alpha.2` exactly. Earlier prerelease lines are preserved as immutable legacy branches and tags."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"The plugin exposes 25 `obsidian_*` tools. Tools, guidance, and approval policy are injected only int"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"o the agent whose message matches the configured trigger vocabulary; unrelated agents do not receive"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"hose message matches the configured trigger vocabulary; unrelated agents do not receive the schemas."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Current release line: `dsh-obsidian-v0.4.0`, built for DSH `dsh-v0.1.2-alpha.2`. DSH alpha.2 is publ"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"ished under npm dist-tag `alpha`; `latest` and `next` still resolve to `0.1.1-rc.2`. Use the exact v"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"ersion for reproducible installations."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Capabilities"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"**Vault tools, available without Obsidian:**"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"`obsidian_status` · `obsidian_list` · `obsidian_stat` · `obsidian_read` · `obsidian_write` · `obsidi"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"an_edit` · `obsidian_append` · `obsidian_mkdir` · `obsidian_copy` · `obsidian_move` · `obsidian_dele"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"edit` · `obsidian_append` · `obsidian_mkdir` · `obsidian_copy` · `obsidian_move` · `obsidian_delete`"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"The filesystem layer uses vault-relative paths, canonical realpath containment, protected dot direct"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"ories, atomic writes, serialized appends, SHA-256 revisions, optimistic `if_match` conflicts, binary"},{"id":"p9s3","text":" size limits, cancellation, and internal trash by default."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"**Knowledge and Obsidian semantic tools:**"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"`obsidian_search` · `obsidian_metadata` · `obsidian_frontmatter_update` · `obsidian_link_resolve` · "},{"id":"p11s2","text":"`obsidian_links` · `obsidian_link_insert`"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"Search is bounded and paginated. Metadata, frontmatter processing, backlinks, unresolved links, and "},{"id":"p12s2","text":"Obsidian-generated links use the companion's native APIs when available."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"**Attachments:**"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"`obsidian_attachment_add` · `obsidian_attachment_read`"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"Attachments accept an alpha.2 durable image reference or a vault-relative source path. Host absolute"},{"id":"p15s2","text":" paths, URLs, dot directories, unbounded binary payloads, and raw binary model output are rejected."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"**Editor and command tools, requiring the companion:**"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"`obsidian_active` · `obsidian_inline_edit` · `obsidian_open` · `obsidian_commands_list` · `obsidian_"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"command` · `obsidian_notice`"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"Inline edits carry the active path, document revision, selection offsets, and expected text. A concu"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"rrent user edit or note switch returns a conflict instead of overwriting content."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"First install DSH `0.1.2-alpha.2` explicitly. Do not rely on npm `latest` or `next` for this line:"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Install the host package into the profile that runs the agent:"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"Replace `<profile>` with the profile you actually boot, such as `web` or `headless`. Alpha.2 profile"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"s record `dsh.profile.patchReload`: `web` uses `live`; shipped `headless`, `acp`, `sdk`, and `sdk-mi"},{"id":"p24s3","text":"nimal` profiles use `startup`. Restart startup-only profiles after adding or changing the plugin."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"Verify the composed tree without booting:"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"The output must contain the `ui-obsidian` row."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"The host package and Obsidian companion are separate artifacts. Install the companion from a checkou"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"t or unpacked host tarball:"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p30s1","text":"A standalone `dsh-obsidian-bridge-0.4.0.zip` is attached to the GitHub Release. Extract only `main.j"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"s` and `manifest.json` into `<vault>/.obsidian/plugins/dsh-obsidian-bridge/`, enable the plugin, and"},{"id":"p30s3","text":" reload Obsidian. Verify hashes against `SHA256SUMS` before installation."},{"id":"p31s1","text":"The companion stores its random token in local plugin `data.json`. The host reads it automatically o"},{"id":"p31s2","text":"nly when `vaultPath` resolves to the same canonical vault. Host and companion major/minor versions m"},{"id":"p31s3","text":"ust match; IPC protocol remains version 1."},{"id":"p32s1","text":"## Configuration"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"The `obsidian` settings namespace applies live when the optional DSH settings provider is mounted:"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"Alpha.2 settings integration uses `ctx.inject(['settings'])` and `settings.installSection(...)`; wit"},{"id":"p35s2","text":"hout a provider the plugin keeps using its profile entry configuration. Secret fields stay write-onl"},{"id":"p35s3","text":"y on redacted settings surfaces."},{"id":"p36s1","text":"## Architecture and alpha.2 changes"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"- `src/index.ts`: optional alpha.2 settings service wiring, runtime lifecycle, skill facade, and per"},{"id":"p37s2","text":"-agent activation.\n- `src/activation.ts`: trigger matching, 25-tool scoped injection, approval polic"},{"id":"p37s3","text":"y, and reversible disposers.\n- `src/vault/`: canonical path boundary and persistent `VaultFs`.\n- `sr"},{"id":"p37s4","text":"c/bridge/`: authenticated JSON Lines IPC, version-line enforcement, and vault identity verification."},{"id":"p37s5","text":"\n- `companion/`: desktop-only Obsidian plugin using a Windows named pipe or Unix socket.\n- `src/tool"},{"id":"p37s6","text":"s/`: Vault, knowledge, attachment, link, editor, and command definitions."},{"id":"p38s1","text":"Alpha.2 retains `execute(args, exec)`, `exec.signal`, scoped `agent.ctx`, `tools/pre-execute`, `skil"},{"id":"p38s2","text":"ls.register`, and `systemPrompt.section`. It moves settings installation onto `ctx.settings`, moves "},{"id":"p38s3","text":"`JsonValue` to `@deepseek-ai/dsh-util-values`, renames tool presentation `code` mode to `ptc`, and r"},{"id":"p38s4","text":"emoves API Proxy. This plugin uses neither presentation-mode names nor API Proxy, so those changes r"},{"id":"p38s5","text":"equire no compatibility shim."},{"id":"p39s1","text":"See ARCHITECTURE.md, MIGRATION.md, SECURITY.md, and CHANGELOG.md."},{"id":"p40s1","text":"## Compatibility"},{"id":"p41s1","text":"| dsh-obsidian | DSH host | Companion | Obsidian | Status |"},{"id":"p42s1","text":"| `0.4.x` / `dsh-obsidian-v0.4.0` | `0.1.2-alpha.2` | `0.4.x` | Desktop `>=1.4.0` | Supported |\n| `0"},{"id":"p42s2","text":".3.x` / `dsh-obsidian-v0.3.1` | `0.1.0-rc.8` | `0.3.x` | Desktop `>=1.4.0` | `legacy/dsh-rc8` |\n| `0"},{"id":"p42s3","text":".2.x` / `dsh-obsidian-v0.2.0` | `0.1.0-rc.7` | `0.2.x` | Desktop `>=1.4.0` | `legacy/dsh-rc7` |\n| `0"},{"id":"p42s4","text":".1.x` / `v0.1.0` | rc.6 line | `0.1.x` | Desktop `>=1.4.0` | `legacy/dsh-rc6` |\n| any other cross-li"},{"id":"p42s5","text":"ne combination | unsupported | unsupported | any | Unsupported |"},{"id":"p43s1","text":"## Security"},{"id":"p44s1","text":"The companion never requests a URL. It listens only on OS-local IPC, requires a random 32-byte token"},{"id":"p44s2","text":", uses constant-time comparison, caps messages at 1 MiB, and verifies canonical vault identity befor"},{"id":"p44s3","text":"e operations. Vault tools fail closed on traversal, absolute paths, control characters, protected do"},{"id":"p44s4","text":"t directories, symlink/junction escapes, stale revisions, oversized payloads, unauthorized commands,"},{"id":"p44s5","text":"link/junction escapes, stale revisions, oversized payloads, unauthorized commands, and cancellation."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
